    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into June 18th looking to capitalize on high-ceiling matchups, led by **Jacob Wilson** and **Gunnar Henderson**. **Jacob Wilson** represents our strongest play at a 67.97 efficiency, buoyed significantly by a favorable matchup against Ryan Johnson\u2019s 5.29 xERA. The park factors provide a 10% lift, and with a plus-matchup against the starter\u2019s skill set, he is primed to drive production. **Gunnar Henderson** follows closely with a 62.18 score; despite facing a capable arm in Woo, his elite placement in the two-hole and a strong platoon advantage keep him firmly in the \"Strong\" start tier. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains a staple at 59.38, providing high-floor stability even against a difficult test in Sonny Gray.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involves **Josh Jung**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 42.87 score. While **Josh Jung** carries a respectable projection, his effectiveness is hampered by a difficult matchup against Joe Ryan\u2014an elite arm with a 3.25 xERA\u2014leading the optimizer to prioritize the higher-upside matchups offered by **Jacob Wilson** and **Miguel Vargas**. Speaking of **Miguel Vargas**, he remains an intriguing start at 52.64; while his raw numbers are moderate, the slow delivery of Weathers creates a unique \"SB-plus\" environment, netting him a 2% boost for stolen base potential. We remain cautious with **Nolan Schanuel** (56.87), as his status is currently tethered to a \"Lineup Pending\" designation; should he shift from the #3 spot or be shuffled lower in the order, his efficiency score is subject to further regression.",
